le is actively working they're  trying to convert this trust into an etf  now there's a lot of people who want  them to issue some sort of uh redemption  functionality uh or allow that there's  other people who say look just convert  it to an etf but the big hurdle to  converting gbtc into an etf is the  regulators the sec they have not  approved a spot bitcoin etf yet they  only have that derivative-based on and  so ultimately what we are watching is a  waiting game how long will it take for  the sec and other regulators to actually  go ahead and approve a bitcoin etf in  the spot market then how long will it  take for them to approve grayscale to  convert the grayscale bitcoin trust gbtc  into an etf once that happens you would  expect to see a return to nav almost  immediately and of course anyone who'd  holding the asset then that would be  positive for them we have a couple of  quotes first with the director of  research and cio at etf trends he said  there's still no way for bitcoin to ever  leave gbtc which means it should  continue to trade with a substantial  discount to reflect that illiquidity  grayscale i think has like three or  three and a half percent of all bitcoin  in circulation inside that fund then the  president of spectral markets gbtc keeps  breaking hearts as the discount widens  gbtc is basically a binary bet on a  physical etf at this point tempting but  tempting the way value traps can be  tempting so obviously he ain't so  excited  then we have james seyfried who  obviously has been on the podcast before  he broke down what would happen if it  was converted to a spot etf he said gbtc  is still trading at a massive discount  around 26.3 percent many think this  means a 26 return if the fund converts  to an etf but the return is actually  much bigger eliminating a 26.5 discount  would be analogous to a security  appreciating to 100 from  73. uh 73.50  which is a 36  return there's no guarantee this  discount will ever collapse or that the  